From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:45:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SableOS: Key remapping in Settings > Keyboard

2.0 plan, key remapping (an idea from q25toolbox's Key Remapper; no code
taken): Settings > Keyboard > Key remapping turns the Q25's $ key, right
Shift or Recents key into Ctrl, Alt, Tab, Esc, Menu or Search in every
app, or gives it its own job back with Default. It uses InputManager's
own key remapping (Settings holds REMAP_MODIFIER_KEYS), which the system
stores and restores at boot, so no keylayout is rewritten and no root is
needed. Keyboard-first rows; the choices are in SableKeyRemap,
unit-tested.
---
 AndroidManifest.xml                           |   6 +
 res/values/sable_key_remap_strings.xml        |  41 ++++++
 res/xml/keyboard_settings.xml                 |  12 ++
 .../android/settings/sable/SableKeyRemap.java |  72 +++++++++++
 .../settings/sable/SableKeyRemapActivity.java | 118 ++++++++++++++++++
 5 files changed, 249 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 res/values/sable_key_remap_strings.xml
 create mode 100644 src/com/android/settings/sable/SableKeyRemap.java
 create mode 100644 src/com/android/settings/sable/SableKeyRemapActivity.java

